module Core

### The protocol for values that can produce an independent duplicate of themselves via `duplicate`.
### `Copyable` is the BROADER capability; `Assignable obeys Copyable` is the STRONGER, narrower one:
### every assignable value is duplicate-able, with `duplicate` DEFAULTING to `assign` (for a managed leaf
### the refcount-share IS the independent copy — the buffer is immutable, shared safely). The reverse
### does NOT hold: an aggregate `entity` (List/Dict) is `Copyable` (heap deep-clone) but NOT `Assignable`
### (single-owner, cannot be shallow-shared — moved via `steal`, never implicitly bound). `duplicate` is
### inserted wherever an independent duplicate is required (e.g. building a value into a collection).
protocol Copyable
needs Copyable everywhere
  ### Returns an independent duplicate of this value (a deep copy for an aggregate; the refcount-share
  ### `assign` for an Assignable managed leaf, which is independent since the buffer is immutable).
  ### :returns: A duplicate of this value with its own valid lifetime and invariants.
  @readonly
  routine Me.duplicate() -> Me
